                    "Recreational land is valued for an experience and the conditions that make it repeatable. Water, habitat, views, trails, seclusion, access, season, neighbors, and maintenance can matter more than acreage. A buyer may seek a retreat, hunting land, a campground, or a future subdivision option. Define the user and price only the features that are legally available and physically usable. Comparable sales, a use-based value, or both may work. Do not borrow the price of a different land type because a listing uses similar language.",
